to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-12 : List (List Word)
to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-12 = cons "- **The ignored basic: equality.** Computing has no account of when two things are the same: the" (cons (quoted (cons "  photo on the phone, in iCloud and in a friend's messages; " (cons "Dad" (cons " in contacts, in a bank's transfer" nil)))) (cons "  list and in photos; version 3 and version 4 of a document; one note edited offline by two people." (cons "  Each system answers with its own rule (a filename, a database key, a hash, a timestamp," (cons "  last-writer-wins), the rules disagree, and none distinguishes identical, equivalent and related by" (cons "  a change. Deduplication, identity across services, syncing, merging, versioning and caching all" (cons "  reinvent a bad equality. The paper begins with identity because it is the basic that was skipped." nil))))))
